Online data sources (fetched at run time, not bundled)
------------------------------------------------------
Live Data screens call public APIs. Each has its own terms; you are responsible for using
them within those terms (polling intervals in the code are deliberately modest):
NOAA/NWS api.weather.gov, NOAA SWPC, NOAA CO-OPS tides, USGS earthquakes and Water Data,
Open-Meteo (air quality; free tier is non-commercial), OpenSky Network (non-commercial
research terms), wheretheiss.at, CelesTrak, HamQSL (N0NBH), GitHub REST API, Yahoo Finance
chart endpoints (unofficial; may break or be restricted), Coinbase / CoinGecko, Frankfurter
(ECB rates), RSS feeds you configure (NPR, BBC, OPB, Ars Technica, ARRL, Reddit and others:
headlines belong to their publishers), Hacker News API, and the X API (needs your own token).
